This is a different session's in-progress admin sidebar/header migration (consistent with
docs/backlog.md's "878 - 879 ... owner's header audit, D81-7" line) landing live in the same working
tree while the locale-leak scan read the Storybook story list. Deleting `AdminSidebar.stories.tsx`,
`AdminMobileHeader.stories.tsx` and `AdminLayout.stories.tsx` mid-scan is the most likely cause of the
scan's exit 127 (a story the scan had already enumerated disappeared before it could render it).

Immediately after, a plain `tasklist` process-list command (no build, no browser) took long enough to be
moved to background by the 120s timeout and produced an implausible ~1.6 million lines of output,
confirming the machine was under severe, abnormal load at that moment from something other than this
session's own work.

